
Use Cloud Scheduler to keep the primary API warm during business hours without
paying for a dedicated instance overnight.

Production:
gcloud scheduler jobs create http ocotillo-api-business-hours-warmup \
  --location=us-west4 \
  --schedule="*/5 8-18 * * 1-5" \
  --time-zone="America/Denver" \
  --uri="https://ocotillo-api-dot-waterdatainitiative-271000.appspot.com/_ah/warmup" \
  --http-method=GET

Staging:
gcloud scheduler jobs create http ocotillo-api-staging-business-hours-warmup \
  --location=us-west4 \
  --schedule="*/5 8-18 * * 1-5" \
  --time-zone="America/Denver" \
  --uri="https://ocotillo-api-staging-dot-waterdatainitiative-271000.appspot.com/_ah/warmup" \
  --http-method=GET
